# VIGIL Red-Pen System-review scheduler — config for vigil-redpen-schedule.service   (reserves review credits)
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/redpen-schedule.env with mode 0600 (`install -m 600 …`). NEVER commit it. This unit holds no
# secret of its own: it signs with the owner key the cockpit's SIGIL_HOME already holds.
# Only the scheduler process receives this file's values: the unit's heartbeat hook runs with an allow-listed env.
# =====================================================================
# Paths in THIS file must be ABSOLUTE (systemd does NOT expand %h inside an EnvironmentFile value; the CLI refuses a
# relative / %-bearing SIGIL_HOME).

# REQUIRED to run at all (Red-Pen is DEFAULT-OFF and the pass refuses without it). Also set it in
# ~/.config/vigil/alerts.env so `vigil alerts` watches this unit fail-closed from the start.
# VIGIL_REDPEN_ENABLED=1

# REQUIRED, ALWAYS — even if you never moved it: the cockpit's SIGIL_HOME, as an absolute path (GO-LIVE §2; outside
# ~/.sigil, also add it to the unit's ReadWritePaths). The pass reserves reviews and signs schedule records on the spine
# under it. It never falls back to ~/.sigil: without this line it REFUSES (the unit goes FAILED). It also refuses when
# ~/.sigil/cockpit.env names a different SIGIL_HOME, or when this directory holds no owner identity.
# Never moved: SIGIL_HOME=/home/USER/.sigil
# SIGIL_HOME=/mnt/vigil-data/.sigil

# OPTIONAL: the seam base, ONLY if the cockpit and the settle drain use another one than the unit's default
# (%h/.sigil/credit-lease). It must be the SAME directory they use — the pass refuses to write a ticket anywhere else —
# and the integration drain (`vigil redpen-schedule --base-dir …`) must read that same directory.
# VIGIL_BASE_DIR=/mnt/vigil-data/.sigil/credit-lease

# PAIRING: this pass only RESERVES a due review and drops its ticket. On the offense/integration plane, run the drain
# that turns tickets into queued jobs — `vigil redpen-schedule --base-dir <the seam above> --watch` — next to the job
# runner. Without it NO System review ever runs, and each reserved review's credits stay held until the W2 reservation
# path releases them (`sigil ops-sweep reservations` refunds a reservation only once a later review of the SAME
# repository supersedes it and its lease window has passed) — so enable this timer only together with the drain.
